<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Reting Rinpoche</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1912–1947</span> · Also known as Thubten Jampal Yeshe Gyaltsen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Reting Rinpoche, the fifth holder of the title, Thubten Jampal Yeshe Gyaltsen, was regent of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a> from 1934 to 1941. He led the search that identified the Fourteenth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dalai-lama">Dalai Lama</a> and presided over his enthronement in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a> in 1940. After resigning in favour of Taktra Rinpoche, he was accused of plotting to return to power and died in prison in Lhasa in 1947.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/reting-rinpoche.jpg" alt="Reting Rinpoche" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ernst Schäfer · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_Bild_135-S-12-40-25,_Tibetexpedition,_Regent_von_Tibet.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
